        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.845,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "same values for any given value of u. But we can see that they do not. So, these two expressions are not equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.136,
            0.625,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "Are the expressions 10y – 3 and 10(y – 3) equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.114,
            0.905,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.166,
            0.735,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "10y – 3, short for 10 × y – 3, means 3 less than 10 times y,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.185,
            0.777,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "10(y – 3), short for 10 × (y – 3), means 10 times (3 less than y)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.204,
            0.847,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "Let us compare the values that these expressions take for different values of y."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.255,
            0.844,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.469,
            0.846,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.528,
            0.64,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "**Example 11:** What is the sum of the numbers in the picture (unknown values are denoted by letter-numbers)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.515,
            0.844,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.549,
            0.75,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.592,
            0.64,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": "There are many ways to go about it. Here, we show some of them."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.587,
            0.749,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.634,
            0.447,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "1. Adding row wise gives:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.657,
            0.624,
            0.845,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.658,
            0.651,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "(4 \\times 3) + (r + s) + (r + s) + (4 \\times 3)",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.687,
            0.543,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": "2. Adding like terms together gives:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.712,
            0.611,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": "( 8 \\times 3 ) + ( r + r ) + ( s + s )",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.741,
            0.633,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": "3. Adding the upper half and doubling gives:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.765,
            0.582,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "2 \\times ( 4 \\times 3 + r + s )",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.79,
            0.847,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "The three expressions might seem different. We can simplify each one and see that they all are the same: 2r + 2s + 24."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.835,
            0.293,
            0.859
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
